Changes made: the following were extracted from the WN-LMF XML release:
single-token noun lemmas, lower-cased (src/nouns.txt); lemmas containing a
space were dropped; lemmas written only with capital letters were kept in a
separate list of known words (src/names.txt); and the irregular noun forms,
as (form, lemma) pairs, unfiltered; and single-token lemmas of the other
parts of speech other than noun (verbs, adjectives, adverbs; WordNet files
interjections such as "alas" as adverbs) that end in "s", lower-cased, kept
in src/others.txt and used only to recognise words WordNet lists as non-nouns.
Everything is written out sorted by byte order to src/data.rs, src/nouns.txt,
src/names.txt and src/others.txt. No other WordNet data
is used. The hand-written policy lists in src/policy.rs are not WordNet data;
they are crate source under the Apache-2.0 licence.

